; Room 47 ($2F): Empty room titled "["
;
; Format: see #R$C000. An empty room: the layout is all background, the name
; is the single character "[" surrounded by spaces, the tile area holds zeros
; followed by bytes that look like Z80 code (not a valid set of tiles), the
; border byte is $7E (low 3 bits: yellow), $DF-$E0 hold $FE,$2C and the entity
; list is empty ($FF in slot 0). The unused tile bytes are harmless as long as
; no cell uses a tile other than 0.
; .
; Exits: left Room 29 (The Nightmare Room, #R$DD00); right byte 205 = $CD,
; page $CD = Room 13 (Out on a limb, #R$CD00); up Room 28 (First Landing,
; #R$DC00); down Room 43 (Conservatory Roof, #R$EB00).
; .
; Entered only from the right exit of Room 46 (Tree Root, #R$EE00), whose
; right edge is walled in, so no way to enter it by walking was found
; (inferred from the layout). Observed: starting in this room from a snapshot,
; Willy falls out through the bottom into Room 43 within 40 frames.
@label=RoomBracket
b$EF00 DEFB $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00 ; row 0: ................................
 $EF08 DEFB $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00 ; row 1: ................................
